    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"The Guide for Writing Word Documents in\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"for Publication in the EPiC Series Andrei Voronkov1,2 and Kryštof Hoder1 1 EasyChair 2 University of Manchester, Manchester, U.K. andrei@voronkov.com, hoderk@cs.man.ac.uk Abstract In order to ease the\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"and similar tools for creating documents for EasyChair-based electronic and on-paper publishing of workshop and conference proceedings. Introduction The styles and parameters of this guide are designe\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \". This guide explains how to produce the docx format in\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \". To achieve high quality of volumes, both LaTeX and Word documents should have the same layout and similar styles. This guide is provided for the users of\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"and describes EasyChair style version 3.4. Document Header The empty space on top of the first page, just before the title, will be reserved for a page header containing the EasyChair and EPiC Series \"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"menu and set the spacing before the paragraph to 94pt and after to 15pt. Styles To produce a document complying with the EasyChair style you can simply take this guide and modify it. Several Word docu\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"you can use the Formatting Palette. The first line should contain the title of the document and be in the style Title. This line should be followed by a line in the style Authors, which specifies auth\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"or other tools able to process docx documents. In\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \", commands for inserting citations are located at the Document Elements tab of the ribbon control in the section References. Clicking the Manage button opens a toolbox, which allows you to add referen\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"for Mac, open the main toolbox and select the Citation tab instead. From there you can add and insert referenced publications as in other versions of Word. The references (or the bibliography) section\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"Microsoft Word\"",
    "                          span",
    "                            span  \"for Mac). After inserting this section, the style of its header should be set to References. The automatically generated References section may need to be explicitly updated to reflect further changes\"",
